or the discovery of new drugs, but another great invention, the microscope.

451
00:37:29,560 --> 00:37:36,520
It was not until the invention of the microscope that scientists were able to detect and defeat deadly bacteria.

452
00:37:37,320 --> 00:37:42,740
While the practice of health care in one form or another is as old as civilization itself,

453
00:37:42,741 --> 00:37:50,740
Early scientists were truly working in the dark until they began applying the principles of optics and lenses to their research.

454
00:37:50,741 --> 00:38:00,740
In 1609 an optician's apprentice discovered that if spectacle lenses were placed in certain positions, objects seen through them appeared to be much closer.

455
00:38:00,741 --> 00:38:08,740
Famed inventor and scientist Galileo vastly improved the invention prompted by this discovery, the telescope.

456
00:38:08,741 --> 00:38:13,560
By creating a device that could magnify objects 30 times their normal size,

457
00:38:14,060 --> 00:38:18,900
Galileo used the telescope to make numerous important discoveries about our solar system.

458
00:38:19,300 --> 00:38:24,860
He soon gazed inward instead of outward with another recently invented optical device

459
00:38:24,861 --> 00:38:28,480
that he said made flies look as big as a lamb.

460
00:38:28,481 --> 00:38:30,900
That device was the microscope.

461
00:38:32,340 --> 00:38:35,760
As man's understanding of optics continued to progress,

462
00:38:35,761 --> 00:38:38,800
microscopes became increasingly powerful.

463
00:38:39,700 --> 00:38:43,560
Aided by the microscope, scientists would uncover life-saving discoveries

464
00:38:43,561 --> 00:38:47,740
that would impact health care more deeply than at any time in history.

465
00:38:48,400 --> 00:38:53,300
They would wage a war with disease armed with a powerful new weapon, vaccines.

466
00:38:54,380 --> 00:38:59,980
It is only because of the microscope that scientists were ultimately able to save millions of lives

467
00:38:59,981 --> 00:39:01,860
with the creation of vaccines.

468
00:39:01,861 --> 00:39:15,180
I mean, a big step forward as far as other vaccines was the microscope and the ability to identify bacteria that were causing diseases, for example, diphtheria.

469
00:39:15,420 --> 00:39:25,600
People were able to see specific organisms, and then they were able to take them and put them into animals and reproduce diseases and show the same organisms.

470
00:39:25,601 --> 00:39:32,400
So the microscope played a major role in the subsequent development of many vaccines.

471
00:39:32,840 --> 00:39:39,580
The earliest recorded attempts to vaccinate against disease dates back to India in 700 AD.

472
00:39:40,560 --> 00:39:44,800
Buddhist monks routinely ingested snake venom in the belief that if they were bitten,

473
00:39:45,280 --> 00:39:48,240
their bodies would have to build up immunity to the poison.

474
00:39:49,080 --> 00:39:52,860
No one knows for certain if that radical attempt at early vaccination was effective,

475
00:39:52,861 --> 00:39:54,880
but they did have the right idea.

476
00:39:55,600 --> 00:39:59,440
But it was not until the end of the 19th century with the help of the microscope

477
00:39:59,441 --> 00:40:03,320
that the link between germs, bacteria and disease was discovered.

478
00:40:04,180 --> 00:40:06,980
Scientists began to create appropriate vaccines.

479
00:40:08,000 --> 00:40:12,120
Vaccines are designed to introduce a bit of the disease into the body

480
00:40:12,121 --> 00:40:14,700
without actually passing on the disease itself.

481
00:40:14,701 --> 00:40:20,060
The body then produces an antibody that creates immunity to the disease in question.

482
00:40:20,900 --> 00:40:26,380
Edward Jenner created the first successful immunization in England in 1796.

483
00:40:27,160 --> 00:40:30,280
And while he was certainly using an early form of the microscope,

484
00:40:30,560 --> 00:40:33,480
his discovery was the result of a keen observation.

485
00:40:34,360 --> 00:40:40,120
Smallpox was an epidemic disease that had plagued the world for more than 2,000 years.

486
00:40:40,780 --> 00:40:43,240
With a mortality rate of over 40%,

487
00:40:43,241 --> 00:40:47,860
scientists were frantically searching for a vaccine to eradicate the deadly disease.

488
00:40:48,600 --> 00:40:54,800
Jenner had observed that if milkmaids on farms got an infection from an illness in cows called cowpox,

489
00:40:55,140 --> 00:40:57,780
they somehow seemed to be immune to smallpox.

490
00:40:58,600 --> 00:41:04,780
What Jenner did was take the material from the lesion of a milkmaid

491
00:41:04,781 --> 00:41:09,680
and inoculated that into the arm of a boy, James Phipps,

492
00:41:09,681 --> 00:41:15,520
and that this boy was subsequently exposed on purpose to smallpox and he was protected.

493
00:41:15,521 --> 00:41:21,280
In time, the once deadly disease smallpox was eradicated completely.

494
00:41:22,340 --> 00:41:29,340
And then, in the late 1800s, French scientist Louis Pasteur made more great strides in vaccine research.

495
00:41:30,920 --> 00:41:38,840
Pasteur is known to history, I think primarily because of the nature of the development of his rabies vaccine.

496
00:41:38,841 --> 00:41:43,840
And that used the attenuated matter to produce a way of treating rabies,

497
00:41:44,500 --> 00:41:47,220
which up until that time, no one had been able to treat.

498
00:41:47,660 --> 00:41:50,640
The next big advancement in medicine was antibiotics.

499
00:41:51,060 --> 00:41:52,780
In the early part of the 20th century,

500
00:41:52,940 --> 00:41:57,500
one of the most important antibiotics in history came close to being shelved forever.

501
00:41:58,220 --> 00:42:01,820
In 1928, penicillin was discovered by Alexander Fleming,

502
00:42:02,180 --> 00:42:06,360
who noticed with the help of microscopes that mold growing on a jelly sample in his lab

503
00:42:06,361 --> 00:42:10,320
completely destroyed bacteria that he had been cultivating.

504
00:42:10,321 --> 00:42:13,800
Ironically, Fleming lost interest in the penicillin discovery,

505
00:42:13,801 --> 00:42:16,800
and it was 10 years before another group of scientists

506
00:42:16,801 --> 00:42:19,860
uncovered his notes, and realizing its potential,

507
00:42:19,861 --> 00:42:23,420
created a form of pure penicillin.

508
00:42:23,421 --> 00:42:25,220
With penicillin, great strides were

509
00:42:25,221 --> 00:42:27,860
being made in the war on bacteria.

510
00:42:27,861 --> 00:42:31,860
But scientists now needed a way to battle viruses.

511
00:42:31,861 --> 00:42:36,040
Viruses, unlike bacteria, are a substance much too small

512
00:42:36,041 --> 00:42:39,800
to be seen by even the strongest conventional microscopes.

513
00:42:39,801 --> 00:42:43,120
Scientists once again harnessed the power of electricity

514
00:42:43,121 --> 00:42:45,540
and created the electron microscope,

515
00:42:45,541 --> 00:42:49,860
a device that finally allowed the magnification of viruses.

516
00:42:49,861 --> 00:42:52,880
America pumped billions of dollars of research money

517
00:42:52,881 --> 00:42:56,420
into the development and creation of new vaccines.

518
00:42:56,421 --> 00:42:59,640
Jonas Salk's research led to the creation of a vaccine

519
00:42:59,641 --> 00:43:03,840
that virtually eradicated the crippling and deadly disease polio.

520
00:43:03,841 --> 00:43:11,580
And a host of other vaccines were created to battle diseases ranging from measles, mumps, rubella, hepatitis, and many others.

521
00:43:12,120 --> 00:43:16,060
These vaccines help us live longer than at any other time in history.

522
00:43:16,780 --> 00:43:22,480
History's key inventions have affected and influenced every aspect of our lives.

523
00:43:22,481 --> 00:43:27,740
How we live, work, play, and travel.

524
00:43:27,741 --> 00:43:34,560
And while these great inventions certainly stand on their own, they are in many ways inextricably connected.

525
00:43:35,420 --> 00:43:39,920
I think what we're seeing in the last 20 or 30 years, the latter part of this decade,

526
00:43:40,100 --> 00:43:45,740
is the amount of technologies that are kind of coming together and being utilized together,

527
00:43:46,580 --> 00:43:53,840
integrated, if you will, is so dramatic that we are seeing advancements unparalleled in any part of history.

528
00:43:53,841 --> 00:43:59,380
the human race has witnessed an incredible wave of important inventions.

529
00:44:00,380 --> 00:44:05,300
As long as man continues to think, he will continue to invent.

530
00:44:06,360 --> 00:44:08,840
And the result will be more great inventions

531
00:44:08,841 --> 00:44:13,100
that will undoubtedly change the course of history.

